  "src": "NAFS Grade 6 \u2022 Test 2 (The Arabian Leopard's Secret Sanctuary)",
  "passage": "The Arabian leopard is one of the rarest big cats on Earth. Once roaming widely across the rugged mountains of Saudi Arabia, its population dropped sharply due to habitat loss and human expansion. Today, dedicated Saudi conservationists are working tirelessly to rescue this magnificent predator from extinction. In the mountains of AlUla and specialized breeding centers in Taif, experts monitor protected habitats and breed captive leopards with the goal of returning them to the wild.\n\nConserving an apex predator like the leopard helps maintain balance in the whole mountain ecosystem. When leopards hunt responsibly, they control populations of wild prey like ibex and rock hyrax, which prevents overgrazing of mountain shrubs. New technological tools, including hidden motion-activated camera traps and satellite GPS collars, allow wildlife rangers to track leopards without disturbing their natural routines. Protecting the Arabian leopard is a national mission that reminds us of the importance of preserving biodiversity."
