  "explain": "In 'Why Sleep Powers the Brain', the correct answer is (B) 'The brain organizes memories and cleanses waste products.'.",
  "src": "NAFS Grade 6 \u2022 Test 2 (Why Sleep Powers the Brain)",
  "passage": "Many students view sleep as merely a pause in their busy day, but scientists know that the brain is extraordinarily active during rest. While your body relaxes, your brain organizes memories, processes information learned during the day, and sweeps away toxic waste products. If you stay up late studying for an exam, you actually impair your ability to remember facts clearly the next morning.\n\nGetting eight to ten hours of quality sleep each night is essential for growing children and teenagers. Adequate rest improves focus, enhances mood, strengthens the immune system, and boosts athletic performance. Doctors recommend creating a peaceful bedtime routine: avoiding bright phone and tablet screens an hour before sleeping, keeping bedroom temperatures cool, and going to bed at the same time every day. Giving your brain sufficient rest is one of the smartest habits for academic success."
