  "src": "NAFS Grade 6 \u2022 Test 3 (The King Salman Science Oasis)",
  "passage": "During their school science excursion, Grade 6 students visited the King Salman Science Oasis in Riyadh. The center features interactive exhibitions designed to inspire curious minds through hands-on experimentation. In the physics gallery, students turned wheels to generate electricity, tested magnetic forces, and launched air-powered rockets to observe acceleration. An enthusiastic museum guide explained how every principle they observed applied to real-world engineering.\n\nNoura was especially fascinated by the water pavilion, where an interactive dam demonstrated how flowing water generates clean hydroelectric power. She recorded observations in her science notebook and asked thoughtful questions about water flow and turbine rotation. Back in class, Noura gave an engaging presentation to her peers, concluding that science is not merely a collection of textbook formulas, but an exciting journey of asking questions and finding answers."
