  "src": "NAFS Grade 6 \u2022 Test 4 (Taif: City of Fragrant Roses)",
  "passage": "Perched high in the Sarawat Mountains, the city of Taif enjoys a refreshing mountain climate that distinguishes it from the hot desert plains below. Taif is world-renowned for its pink Damask roses, which bloom by the millions every spring across terraced mountain slopes. The cool mountain air, mineral-rich soil, and morning dew create the perfect growing environment for these delicate blossoms.\n\nDuring the harvest season in March and April, farmers wake at dawn to hand-pick rose blossoms while the petals are still moist with morning dew. The flowers are immediately taken to traditional distilleries, where copper cauldrons boil the petals with pure water to produce prized rose water and precious rose essential oil, known as attar. It takes thousands of fresh roses to produce a single tiny vial of pure rose oil, making Taif rose oil one of the most treasured fragrances worldwide."
