  "passage": "Al-Balad, the historic district of Jeddah, is a UNESCO World Heritage site that has welcomed traders and pilgrims for over a thousand years. Its distinctive architecture features multi-story houses constructed from Red Sea coral stones and limestone, reinforced with heavy wooden beams. The most eye-catching feature of these historic homes is the roshan, an ornate wooden bay window with delicate lattice screens.\n\nRoshan windows are a brilliant architectural solution designed for both comfort and privacy. The wooden lattice permits cool sea breezes to circulate into living quarters while filtering out harsh sunlight and dust. Residents could look out at the bustling street below without passersby seeing inside. Today, meticulous preservation projects are restoring historic buildings in Al-Balad, transforming them into vibrant museums, art centers, and cultural hubs where history meets the future."
