  "src": "NAFS Grade 6 \u2022 Test 5 (Digital Citizenship for Young Learners)",
  "passage": "The internet connects students to vast libraries of knowledge, educational games, and friends around the globe. However, becoming a skilled internet user involves much more than knowing how to search for websites. It requires practicing positive digital citizenship: treating others with courtesy, protecting private personal data, and thinking critically about information encountered online.\n\nResponsible digital citizens protect their passwords and never share private information like home addresses, phone numbers, or passwords with strangers. They also practice empathy by posting only kind comments, remembering that real people with feelings read their messages. Finally, young digital citizens verify information before sharing, knowing that misleading rumors can spread rapidly. Navigating the web with wisdom and kindness ensures that technology remains a force for good."
